The superhit Tamil film Leo, directed by Lokesh Kanagaraj and starring ‘Thalapathy’ Vijay, has now entered the home stretch of its box office run, less than two weeks after its release. 
Like most tent pole Tamil-language movies, Leo was also frontloaded, but has taken a nosedive in daily collections despite having passed major domestic and worldwide milestones. 
On day 12 of release, Leo made an estimated Rs 45 crore across India, according to industry tracker Sacnilk.
This takes the movie’s nett domestic collection to Rs 308 crore. 
Overall occupancy for the Tamil-language version was 21%, while Telugu occupancy stood at 28% and the Hindi version reported day 12 occupancy of less than 10%. 
Leo opened to Rs 64 crore on day one, a Thursday, breaking the record for Tamil cinema this year.
